# Code owners (T-13d plan gate, Q4 — owner decision, 2026-09-25: "Codeowner kimi məni göstər").
# governance.md's Roles table names one Owner (Ruslan) and no other reviewer; the GitHub
# collaborator list confirms it (one collaborator, @wdaz, admin — read live during T-13d's
# planning, docs/04-process/plans/2026-09-25-T-13d.md, Finding F7). This file names that owner
# for every path so a required-review branch rule has someone to route to.
#
# It enforces nothing by itself: GitHub only requires a code-owner review when a branch
# ruleset's "Require review from Code Owners" setting is also on. Read from GitHub's API on
# 2026-09-25 (`gh api repos/wdaz/ai-native-personal-finance/rules/branches/main`): that setting
# (`require_code_owner_review`) is off in the `main` ruleset. Leave it off: the only code owner
# is also the author of every pull request, and GitHub does not count an author's approval of
# their own pull request (GitHub's documented rule; not tested here), so with no bypass actor in
# the ruleset (none today) turning it on would block every merge.
